# This file is both this repo's credentials template and the routing template
# paired with the published sandbar.config.example.mjs (#39, #137). Copy it to
# `sandbar.env` — which is gitignored — beside the config that will read it.
#
# Both configs call `splitRoleRouting` on this file before assigning
# `config.env`: the twenty-four `SANDBAR_*` keys below become this installation's
# per-role routing and never enter a sandbox, while everything else is the
# credential allowlist every agent container receives.
#
# Not `.env`: that filename at a repo root is already spoken for by compose,
# Vite, Next and Laravel, and sandbar names no file of its own (#38).
#
# A key left EMPTY here is inherited from the process environment instead, so
# `GH_TOKEN=` means "take it from my shell" and CI needs no file at all.

# Required. Every `gh` call — the planner's issue list, the finalise comments
# and label flips, the merger's closes — authenticates with this. Needs `repo`
# scope (classic) or Contents+Issues+Pull-requests read/write (fine-grained).
GH_TOKEN=

# Exactly one of the two below. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY takes precedence if both are
# set. Sandbar's preflight refuses to start with neither.
#
# Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise subscription; generate with `claude setup-token`:
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Pay-as-you-go API key:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional per-installation role routing (#137). These values override the
# driver's defaults without making sandbar.config.mjs dirty: claude everywhere;
# implementer and reviewer (and so adjudicator) on "opus" at `high`; the UI
# check on "sonnet" at `high`; the quality pass on "sonnet" at `medium`; the
# merger on "opus" at `medium`; the thread condenser on the quality pass's
# CLI, "sonnet" on claude, at the CLI's default effort; the scenario writer on
# "opus" at the CLI's default effort; `npm run reflect`'s
# tagger on "sonnet" at `medium` and its synthesizer on "opus" at `high`.
# Leave a key absent or empty to keep the default; this repo's own hosts set
# none.
# Move an agent and its model id together: resolveConfig refuses a non-claude
# role that inherits a claude alias. A codex role should also name its effort:
# the sandbox reads no host config.toml, so an unset effort runs at the
# server's per-model default — `low` for gpt-5.6-sol (#130).
#
# SANDBAR_IMPLEMENTER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_IMPLEMENTER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_IMPLEMENTER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_UI_CHECK_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_UI_CHECK_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_UI_CHECK_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_QUALITY_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_QUALITY_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_REVIEWER_QUALITY_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_ADJUDICATOR_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_ADJUDICATOR_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_ADJUDICATOR_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_CONDENSER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_CONDENSER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_CONDENSER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_WRITER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_WRITER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_WRITER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_RUNNER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_RUNNER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_SCENARIO_RUNNER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_MERGER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_MERGER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_MERGER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_TAGGER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_TAGGER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_TAGGER_EFFORT=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_SYNTHESIZER_AGENT=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_SYNTHESIZER_MODEL_ID=
# SANDBAR_REFLECT_SYNTHESIZER_EFFORT=
